          "width": 257,
          "height": 387
        },
        "pageimage": "IainMBanksLooktoWindward.jpg",
        "extract": "Look to Windward is a science fiction novel by Scottish writer Iain M. Banks, first published in 2000. It is Banks' sixth published novel to feature the Culture. The book's dedication reads: \"For the Gulf War Veterans\".\nThe novel takes its title from a line in T. S. Eliot's poem The Waste Land:\n\nLook to Windward is loosely a sequel to Consider Phlebas, Banks's first published Culture novel. Consider Phlebas took its name from the following line in the poem and dealt with the events of the Idiran-Culture War; Look to Windward deals with the results of the war on those who lived through it.",
        "pageprops": {
