        "title": "Free fall",
        "extract": "In classical mechanics, free fall is any motion of a body where gravity is the only force acting upon it.\nA freely falling object may not necessarily be falling down in the vertical direction. If the common definition of the word \"fall\" is used, an object moving upwards is not considered to be falling, but using scientific definitions, if it is subject to only the force of gravity, it is said to be in free fall.  The Moon is thus in free fall around the Earth, though its orbital speed keeps it in very far orbit from the Earth's surface.\nIn a roughly uniform gravitational field, gravity acts on each part of a body approximately equally.  When there...",
